meta {
  name: Validation
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  Every way the create endpoint says no. All of these return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails with
  a 400 and an `errors` object keyed by field name, which is what `ValidationProblem`
  produces from `ModelState`.

  Two things to know before reading the assertions:

  - **The controller returns on the first problem it finds**, so a request with several
    faults reports only one. These requests each break exactly one rule for that reason.
  - **Error keys come from two places and are cased differently.** Keys the controller
    adds by hand are PascalCase (`Payload`, `ExpiresInSeconds`) because they come from
    `nameof`; keys the framework adds during model binding are JSON paths
    (`$.expiresInSeconds`). Anything parsing these has to handle both.

  These requests still consume rate-limit permits — the limiter runs ahead of validation.
  See the collection docs.
}
